	],
	"install": [
		{
			"find": "Invitation",
			"install_to": "GameData"
		}
	],
	"x_netkan_comment": "Not yet submitted to the CKAN metadata repo; users install Invitation manually (see README) while its dependencies come from CKAN. No release_status is set deliberately — with a github $kref it auto-derives from whether the GitHub Release is marked 'pre-release' (leave unchecked for a real release, check it for a testing/beta build). x_netkan_github.use_source_archive is required since releases won't carry a built zip asset — NetKAN pulls the tagged commit's source archive instead, which GitHub wraps in a commit-hash-suffixed folder (e.g. cy6253-ksp-Invitation-a0e9842/GameData/Invitation/...) that changes every release. install uses 'find' (locate the top-most directory named exactly 'Invitation', ignoring the wrapper) rather than 'file' (exact-path match, verified via a real inflate to fail here with 'No files found matching file=\"GameData/Invitation\"'). $kref/homepage/repository point to the real GitHub repo (cy6253/ksp-Invitation); 'author' is the GitHub owner handle — change it to a preferred display name before any CKAN submission. Dependency identifiers verified against public CKAN listings (docs/DEPENDENCIES.md); exact version pins deferred to packaging. GrannusExpansionPack-Primary is a conflict because Invitation requires Kerbin to remain the home system (GEP base variant), not GEP's alternate Grannus-as-home variant. x_screenshot points to the prologue comic (docs/prologue.png)."
}
